Chase H.Q. - Help
=================
This is Chase H.Q., a reconstruction of the ZX Spectrum
version of the 1988 Taito arcade game, released by Ocean
Software in 1989. The game has been rebuilt as portable C
code and runs on the RISC OS desktop.

Compatibility
-------------
* RISC OS 3.1 or later.
* ARM250 or better.

Requirements
------------
The application is built using the GCCSDK toolchain. It
requires the modules CallASWI 0.03 and SharedCLibrary 5.17
or greater to be available in your !System. If you don't
have them, they are available in RISC OS Open Ltd's
'System resources' package:
https://www.riscosopen.org/content/downloads/common

Playing
-------
Click on the iconbar icon to open a game window. Click in
the window to give it the keyboard caret. See 'Instructions'
on the iconbar menu for the keys.

Full screen
-----------
Press F10 or choose Full screen from the View menu. The game
prefers a suitable 4bpp screen mode. To override the choice
set `ChaseHQ$ScreenMode` to a mode number before running
the application. Press Escape to return to the desktop.

Saving
------
Saving is not available for this game.
